From: "Pluet, LLC" <358065800+pluetllc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: optional lossless linear PCM output, and raw PCM
 input for the passthrough sink

APACConfiguration.losslessPCM makes SpatialAudioRenderer enqueue the rendered
speaker feeds as they are: interleaved 32-bit float linear PCM at 48 kHz in
the layout's Atmos channel layout (kAudioChannelLayoutTag_Atmos_7_1_4), in
independent packets of 1024 frames, with no encoder priming. APAC is a lossy
codec (48.4 dB signal-to-error on a film at the default 3.072 Mbit/s); linear
PCM keeps every bit the renderer produced, and the renderer is ready as soon
as it holds audio instead of after the live encoder's 1.5 s. Everything else
(timeline, discard and padding, progress, refill after an automatic flush)
is the APAC path's: an LPCM packet is simply a sync packet. File and HLS
output stay APAC.

SpatialAudioPassthroughSink gains an internal rawPCM mode, for a host that
feeds already decoded PCM through a renderer with its own decoder: the bytes
skip the IEC 61937 unpacker.

---
